readers.already_borrowed:
From prp-spike, already in scout-ahead (docs/prior-art.md 'What was borrowed' plus the checkout):
- kill criteria fixed before the build and re-read before a pivot or close (start, pivot and close skills);
- keep criteria;
- proved/inferred on code decisions, with the inferred ones re-run before the close (decide --proof; close skill step 2);
- the verdict proven/disproven/conditional/unanswered (close --verdict) and 'most honest disproofs are conditional';
- the 'still unknown' list (close --unknown; handoff '## Still unknown');
- 'a working artifact is not a proven hypothesis';
- reconnaissance may sharpen the question, but findings from the artifact must not reshape it (start skill, last line);
- the riskiest direction first (start --direction; also from GSD);
- fair comparison: metric/criteria fixed before any variant exists, one axis, no cherry-picked hybrid, report the losers' strengths (variants skill);
- pre-registration before the scored run (prereg; from agent-lab-kit);
- frame written to disk before the build, so it survives compaction (state.json plus the SessionStart hook);
- propose where the verdict lands, including 'nowhere', and do not file it (handoff skill step 4).

Out of scope as source glue, or against scout-ahead's rules:
- the PRP store resolver ($PRP_DIR, ~/.prp);
- the secret-gist route (an outward publish);
- the tracker routing table (gh issue search);
- 'never opens a PR' (scout has its own kill/commit outcome);
- 'confirm an ambiguous hypothesis before building' in interactive mode (would ask the human);
- the web-researcher and codebase-analyst agents;
- worktree on spike/<slug> (scout already has --worktree and arm worktrees);
- the rule that a validated spike is rewritten rather than carried forward (it contradicts scout's `--outcome commit`; only the effort and untouched-parts disclaimer is proposed).

